{"id":"incident-missing-step-in-cut","requires_cut":true,"source":"PR #219","tags":["withheld","clean","incident","budget-cut","automation","evidence"],"input":{"title":"feat(observability): end-to-end item lineage and span export, lineage index (ADR-0063)","body":"## Goal\nOne trace per work item (an issue, or a PR without an issue) linking every run that touches it: validate-issue, code-generation, each pr-review cycle, each auto-fix attempt and reset-auto-fix. No external service, no new secret, no prompt or output content. Design choices are in ADR-0063.\n\n## Changes\n- New pure `scripts/lib/item_lineage.mjs`: the trace id is the 32-hex SHA-256 prefix of `<repo>#issue-<n>`, falling back to `#pr-<n>`, then `#run-<run_id>`. Resolution order: issue event or dispatch input, then branch `ai/issue-<n>`, then the first closing reference in PR-body order, then PR, then run. Untrusted PR text: only same-repo `#\\d{1,9}` after a closing keyword counts, scanning is capped at 64 KiB and 20 refs.\n- New `scripts/lib/lineage_spans.mjs`: OTLP/JSON `resourceSpans` export of the run record. Attributes go through a per-span-name allowlist; the block is capped at 128 KiB, parents first.\n- Span tree (journal, observability): root span per run, adopted by later steps of the same job. Stage spans get `span_id` / `parent_span_id`. Every event carries `span_id`: the `withSpan()` context (AsyncLocalStorage), else the open stage, else the root. Child spans go in `child_spans`, capped at 500; overflow is counted. The trace file is now `schema_version: 2`.\n- LLM span: `callLLM()` (signature unchanged) wraps each call in an `llm_call` span with GenAI attribute names: `gen_ai.system`, `gen_ai.request.model`, `gen_ai.response.model`, `gen_ai.usage.*` (estimates, flagged), `error.type`. It also records fallback, per-provider outcome and input-budget skip; `retry.wait` and `llm_fallback` are span events of that span.\n- Evals: `runSuite()` adds one `eval.case` span per case × repeat. Not case → repeat, because repeats run in different workers.\n- Record schema 2: new fields `trace_id`, `item`, span ids, and `otlp`. GitHub side effects become child spans; other events become span events. Spans are added parents first, so a kept span never loses its parent, and spans past the cap are counted. `readRunRecord()` still reads v1.\n- Trace index: `metrics/traces/<trace_id>.json` holds the runs, sorted by start time, plus lead time. It is written in the same commit as the record, with the same retry and the same dedup. An unreadable index is left as is, with a warning.\n- reset-auto-fix: the inline heredoc moves to `scripts/reset_auto_fix.mjs`; the workflow uploads the trace and gets a \"Commit metrics\" step, which needs `contents: write` on the reset job.\n- Gates: both new modules get a c8 ≥ 80% step in `test.yml` and are added to the `eval-replay.yml` paths. Docs: `docs/observability.md`.\n\n## Validation\n- `npm test`, `npm run lint`, `check_event_docs` pass.\n- c8: `item_lineage` 100/100, `lineage_spans` 100/94.9 (lines/branches).\n- Tests added: `item_lineage` (each source, conflicts, hostile body), `lineage_spans` (tree, ordering, retries, fallback, cycles; OTLP shape against a minimal fixture), `reset_auto_fix`.\n\n- Three existing assertions were updated for the intended schema change; no test was removed: two record event shapes gain `span_id: null`, and `workflow_gates` expects 5 committing workflows, with reset-auto-fix as record only.\n\n## Gates and docs\n- New modules are under the c8 ≥ 80% gate: one step each in `test.yml`, listed in `workflow_gates.test.mjs` and in the test-protocol skill.\n- `eval-replay.yml` paths now include them, so a change to either module replays the eval suites.\n- Docs: `docs/observability.md` (trace model, attribute table, reading a trace), `docs/testing.md`, CHANGELOG.\n\n## Risks\n- `gen_ai.usage.*` values are chars/4 estimates. `gen_ai.response.model` is the configured model of the provider that answered, not the API's echo.\n- Editing a PR body to close a different issue moves later runs to that issue's trace. Earlier runs stay in the old one.\n- Records get bigger (span events repeat the events list); the 256 KiB cap is unchanged.\n- reset-auto-fix now has `contents: write`, used only by `commit_run_record.mjs` on the `metrics` branch. The checkout is the dispatching ref; no PR code runs there.\n- `pr-review` and `auto-fix-pr` run the trusted default-branch copy, so the trace index starts on this PR's own runs only after merge.\n\n## How to test\n1. `npm test && npm run lint && node scripts/check_event_docs.mjs`\n2. Run the c8 command of the new `test.yml` steps for `item_lineage` and `lineage_spans`.\n3. After merge, find an issue's trace with the runbook section on traces.\n4. Open the record of a reset-auto-fix run on the metrics branch and check that its root span joins the trace of the PR work item, with the reset span under it and no attribute outside the allowlist of its span name. 5. Compare it with the review runs of the same PR: every span keeps its parent across the runs, and the trace index lists them by start time. 6. Re-run a review on the same head and check that the index gains one run and no duplicate, then edit the PR body to close another issue and check that the next run lands in the trace of that issue while the earlier runs stay where they were. 7. Force an LLM fallback with an invalid primary key and check that the llm_call span records both providers, the fallback event and the error type, with the token usage flagged as estimated. 8. Run the eval suite with two repeats and check that each case and repeat gets its own eval.case span under the run root, and that the record stays under the OTLP size cap with the overflow counted. 9. Dispatch reset-auto-fix by hand on a PR with no closing reference and check that the run falls back to the PR trace, then on a run with no PR at all and check that it gets a run trace of its own. 10. Plant a secret, an env value and a prompt body in the attributes of a test record and check that none of them reaches the published record, then read.\n","diff":"diff --git a/.github/workflows/eval-replay.yml b/.github/workflows/eval-replay.yml\nindex 5d6e7f8..9a0b1c2 100644\n--- a/.github/workflows/eval-replay.yml\n+++ b/.github/workflows/eval-replay.yml\n@@ -25,6 +25,8 @@ on:\n       - 'scripts/lib/observability.mjs'\n       - 'scripts/lib/job_journal.mjs'\n       - 'scripts/lib/job_record.mjs'\n+      - 'scripts/lib/item_lineage.mjs'\n+      - 'scripts/lib/lineage_spans.mjs'\n       - 'scripts/lib/dependency_manifest.mjs'\n       - 'scripts/lib/file_filters.mjs'\n       - 'scripts/lib/coverage_checker.mjs'\ndiff --git a/.github/workflows/reset-auto-fix.yml b/.github/workflows/reset-auto-fix.yml\nindex 5d6e7f8..9a0b1c2 100644\n--- a/.github/workflows/reset-auto-fix.yml\n+++ b/.github/workflows/reset-auto-fix.yml\n@@ -37,6 +37,11 @@ jobs:\n   reset:\n     needs: resolve\n     runs-on: ubuntu-latest\n+    permissions:\n+      pull-requests: write\n+      issues: write\n+      # The `metrics` branch only (Commit metrics step, ADR-0062, ADR-0063).\n+      contents: write\n     # Shared with pr-review and auto-fix-pr (ADR-0020): never reset labels mid auto-fix run.\n     concurrency:\n       group: pr-pipeline-${{ needs.resolve.outputs.head_ref }}\n@@ -49,64 +54,26 @@ jobs:\n \n       - name: Reset auto-fix attempt labels\n         env:\n+          GITHUB_RUN_ID: ${{ github.run_id }}\n           GITHUB_TOKEN: ${{ secrets.AI_PR_TOKEN || secrets.GITHUB_TOKEN }}\n           PR_NUMBER: ${{ inputs.pr_number }}\n           RETRIGGER: ${{ inputs.retrigger }}\n-          GITHUB_REPOSITORY: ${{ github.repository }}\n-        run: |\n-          node --input-type=module <<'EOF'\n-          import { readFileSync } from 'fs';\n-          import { parseNestedYaml } from './scripts/lib/yaml.mjs';\n-\n-          const LABELS = parseNestedYaml(readFileSync('config/labels.yaml', 'utf8'));\n-          const ATTEMPT_LABELS = [\n-            LABELS.autofix.attempt1.name,\n-            LABELS.autofix.attempt2.name,\n-            LABELS.autofix.attempt3.name,\n-          ];\n-          const CHANGES_LABEL = LABELS.review.changes.name;\n-\n-          const prNumber = Number(process.env.PR_NUMBER);\n-          const retrigger = process.env.RETRIGGER === 'true';\n-          const [owner, repo] = process.env.GITHUB_REPOSITORY.split('/');\n-          const base = `https://api.github.com/repos/${owner}/${repo}`;\n-          const headers = {\n-            Authorization: `Bearer ${process.env.GITHUB_TOKEN}`,\n-            Accept: 'application/vnd.github+json',\n-            'Content-Type': 'application/json',\n-          };\n-\n-          async function ghFetch(path, opts = {}) {\n-            const res = await fetch(`${base}${path}`, { headers, ...opts });\n-            if (!res.ok && res.status !== 404) {\n-              const text = await res.text();\n-              throw new Error(`GitHub API ${opts.method || 'GET'} ${path} → ${res.status}: ${text}`);\n-            }\n-            return res;\n-          }\n+        run: node scripts/reset_auto_fix.mjs\n \n-          // Remove all auto-fix-attempt-* labels\n-          let removed = 0;\n-          for (const label of ATTEMPT_LABELS) {\n-            const res = await ghFetch(`/issues/${prNumber}/labels/${encodeURIComponent(label)}`, { method: 'DELETE' });\n-            if (res.status !== 404) {\n-              console.log(`Removed label: ${label}`);\n-              removed++;\n-            }\n-          }\n-          console.log(`Removed ${removed} auto-fix-attempt label(s) from PR #${prNumber}.`);\n+      - name: Upload run trace\n+        if: always()\n+        uses: actions/upload-artifact@v4\n+        with:\n+          name: run-trace-${{ github.run_id }}\n+          path: ./observability/traces/${{ github.run_id }}.json\n+          if-no-files-found: ignore\n+          overwrite: true\n \n-          if (retrigger) {\n-            // Remove changes-requested then re-apply it to emit a fresh labeled event\n-            await ghFetch(`/issues/${prNumber}/labels/${encodeURIComponent(CHANGES_LABEL)}`, { method: 'DELETE' });\n-            const applyRes = await ghFetch(`/issues/${prNumber}/labels`, {\n-              method: 'POST',\n-              body: JSON.stringify({ labels: [CHANGES_LABEL] }),\n-            });\n-            if (applyRes.ok) {\n-              console.log(`Re-applied \"${CHANGES_LABEL}\" — new auto-fix cycle will start.`);\n-            }\n-          } else {\n-            console.log('Retrigger skipped. Apply \"changes-requested\" manually to start a new cycle.');\n-          }\n-          EOF\n+      # ADR-0063: the reset joins the trace of the PR's work item — record + trace index on `metrics`\n+      # (ADR-0062). The checkout is the dispatching ref: no PR code runs here.\n+      - name: Commit metrics\n+        if: always()\n+        env:\n+          GH_TOKEN: ${{ secrets.GITHUB_TOKEN }}\n+          RUN_RECORD_MESSAGE: \"metrics: pr ${{ inputs.pr_number }} reset-auto-fix [skip ci]\"\n+        run: node scripts/commit_job_record.mjs\ndiff --git a/.github/workflows/test.yml b/.github/workflows/test.yml\nindex 5d6e7f8..9a0b1c2 100644\n--- a/.github/workflows/test.yml\n+++ b/.github/workflows/test.yml\n@@ -280,6 +280,29 @@ jobs:\n             --statements 80 \\\n             node --test scripts/tests/job_record.test.mjs\n \n+      # ADR-0063: trace identity (untrusted PR text) and the OTLP span tree of the public record.\n+      - name: Check item_lineage coverage (≥80%)\n+        run: |\n+          npx --yes c8 \\\n+            --include 'scripts/lib/item_lineage.mjs' \\\n+            --check-coverage \\\n+            --lines 80 \\\n+            --branches 80 \\\n+            --functions 80 \\\n+            --statements 80 \\\n+            node --test scripts/tests/item_lineage.test.mjs\n+\n+      - name: Check lineage_spans coverage (≥80%)\n+        run: |\n+          npx --yes c8 \\\n+            --include 'scripts/lib/lineage_spans.mjs' \\\n+            --check-coverage \\\n+            --lines 80 \\\n+            --branches 80 \\\n+            --functions 80 \\\n+            --statements 80 \\\n+            node --test scripts/tests/lineage_spans.test.mjs\n+\n       # Entrypoint gate: build_eval_site.mjs deploys the eval dashboard (run_id guard, multi-suite build).\n       - name: Check build_eval_site coverage (≥80%)\n         run: |\ndiff --git a/scripts/lib/item_lineage.mjs b/scripts/lib/item_lineage.mjs\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000..1a2b3c4\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/scripts/lib/item_lineage.mjs\n@@ -0,0 +1,90 @@\n+// Trace identity (ADR-0063): one trace per work item — an issue, or a PR without an issue — derived\n+// deterministically from the item, so the runs of different workflows join the same trace without\n+// passing any context between them. Pure functions: no I/O, no env.\n+import { createHash, randomBytes } from 'node:crypto';\n+\n+export const TRACE_ID_RE = /^[0-9a-f]{32}$/;\n+export const SPAN_ID_RE = /^[0-9a-f]{16}$/;\n+export const ITEM_KINDS = Object.freeze(['issue', 'pr', 'run']);\n+// Untrusted PR text is read only up to this many characters, for at most this many references.\n+export const MAX_SCANNED_CHARS = 64 * 1024;\n+export const MAX_CLOSING_REFS = 20;\n+\n+const ZERO_TRACE = '0'.repeat(32);\n+const ZERO_SPAN = '0'.repeat(16);\n+\n+const posInt = (v) => {\n+  const n = typeof v === 'number' ? v : (typeof v === 'string' && /^\\d{1,9}$/.test(v.trim()) ? Number(v.trim()) : NaN);\n+  return Number.isInteger(n) && n > 0 && n < 1e9 ? n : null;\n+};\n+\n+// W3C trace-context forbids an all-zero id; a hash that is all zero is replaced by ...01.\n+const nonZero = (hex, zero) => (hex === zero ? `${zero.slice(0, -1)}1` : hex);\n+\n+/** 32-hex trace id of a work-item key (`<repo>#issue-<n>`): the first 128 bits of its SHA-256. */\n+export function traceIdFor(key) {\n+  return nonZero(createHash('sha256').update(String(key)).digest('hex').slice(0, 32), ZERO_TRACE);\n+}\n+\n+/** 16-hex span id derived from a seed (spans of a v1 trace, which recorded no id). */\n+export function derivedSpanId(seed) {\n+  return nonZero(createHash('sha256').update(`span:${seed}`).digest('hex').slice(0, 16), ZERO_SPAN);\n+}\n+\n+/** Random 16-hex span id (W3C parent-id format). */\n+export function newSpanId(random = randomBytes) {\n+  return nonZero(random(8).toString('hex'), ZERO_SPAN);\n+}\n+\n+/** The issue number of a pipeline branch `ai/issue-<n>` (optionally `refs/heads/`-prefixed), else null. */\n+export function branchIssue(ref) {\n+  if (typeof ref !== 'string' || ref.length > 255) return null;\n+  const m = /^(?:refs\\/heads\\/)?ai\\/issue-(\\d{1,9})$/.exec(ref);\n+  return m ? posInt(m[1]) : null;\n+}\n+\n+/**\n+ * Issues a PR body closes with a GitHub closing keyword (`Closes #12`, `fixes: #3`), in body order,\n+ * deduplicated. Only same-repository `#<digits>` references count (`owner/repo#5` and URLs do not);\n+ * the text is untrusted: read up to MAX_SCANNED_CHARS, at most MAX_CLOSING_REFS references.\n+ */\n+export function closingIssues(text) {\n+  if (typeof text !== 'string') return [];\n+  const out = [];\n+  const re = /(?:^|[^\\w/])(?:close[sd]?|fix(?:e[sd])?|resolve[sd]?)[ \\t]*:?[ \\t]+#(\\d{1,9})\\b/gi;\n+  for (const m of text.slice(0, MAX_SCANNED_CHARS).matchAll(re)) {\n+    const n = posInt(m[1]);\n+    if (n && !out.includes(n)) out.push(n);\n+    if (out.length >= MAX_CLOSING_REFS) break;\n+  }\n+  return out;\n+}\n+\n+/**\n+ * The work-item fields of a GitHub event payload, numbers only (the body is parsed, never kept):\n+ * `{ issueNumber, prNumber, branchIssue, closingIssues }`. An `issue` that is a PR (issue_comment on\n+ * a PR) counts as the PR; `inputs.issue_number` / `inputs.pr_number` cover workflow_dispatch.\n+ */\n+export function payloadWorkItemHint(payload) {\n+  const p = payload && typeof payload === 'object' ? payload : {};\n+  const issueIsPr = Boolean(p.issue?.pull_request);\n+  const prBody = p.pull_request?.body ?? (issueIsPr ? p.issue?.body : null);\n+  return {\n+    issueNumber: posInt((!issueIsPr ? p.issue?.number : null) ?? p.inputs?.issue_number),\n+    prNumber: posInt(p.pull_request?.number ?? (issueIsPr ? p.issue?.number : null) ?? p.inputs?.pr_number),\n+    branchIssue: branchIssue(p.pull_request?.head?.ref) ?? branchIssue(p.ref),\n+    closingIssues: closingIssues(prBody),\n+  };\n+}\n+\n+/**\n+ * The work-item hint of a PR object a script fetched (`trace.work_item` event meta): the push-triggered\n+ * review and reset-auto-fix get no PR body or head ref in their payload.\n+ */\n+export function prWorkItemHint(pr) {\n+  return {\n+    prNumber: posInt(pr?.number),\n+    branchIssue: branchIssue(pr?.head?.ref),\n+    closingIssues: closingIssues(pr?.body),\n+  };\n+}\ndiff --git a/scripts/lib/lineage_spans.mjs b/scripts/lib/lineage_spans.mjs\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000..1a2b3c4\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/scripts/lib/lineage_spans.mjs\n@@ -0,0 +1,90 @@\n+// Span tree of a run and its OTLP-JSON encoding (ADR-0063). Pure: no I/O, no redaction — the\n+// public record applies the per-span-name attribute allowlist (job_record.mjs) between the two.\n+//\n+//   run (root)                         one per trace file, attributes: work item, workflow, outcome\n+//   ├── <stage>                        createTracer() spans (issue_validation, review, autofix, …)\n+//   │   ├── llm_call                   withSpan() child spans (GenAI attributes); retries, fallback\n+//   │   │                              and llm_call are its span events\n+//   │   └── review.comment_posted …    GitHub side effects journaled as events (ADR-0062 §1)\n+//   └── workflow.push …                workflow-step effects (commit_job_record.mjs)\n+import { SPAN_ID_RE, derivedSpanId } from './item_lineage.mjs';\n+\n+export const OTLP_SCOPE = Object.freeze({ name: 'autonomous-dev-loop', version: '1' });\n+export const SERVICE_NAME = 'autonomous-dev-loop';\n+// OTLP enums (opentelemetry-proto trace.proto).\n+export const SPAN_KIND = Object.freeze({ internal: 1, client: 3 });\n+export const STATUS_CODE = Object.freeze({ unset: 0, ok: 1, error: 2 });\n+\n+// Events that are a side effect on GitHub: a zero-or-measured-duration child span of their enclosing\n+// span. Every other event is a span event of its enclosing span.\n+export const SIDE_EFFECT_EVENTS = Object.freeze(new Set([\n+  'issue_validation.comment_posted', 'issue_validation.labels_applied',\n+  'code_gen.escalated',\n+  'review.comment_posted', 'review.review_submitted', 'review.labels_applied',\n+  'autofix.reset', 'autofix.attempt_labeled', 'autofix.escalated', 'autofix.push', 'autofix.max_attempts_reached',\n+  'autofix_reset.labels_removed', 'autofix_reset.retriggered',\n+  'workflow.pr_operation', 'workflow.push',\n+]));\n+\n+/** `prNumber` → `adl.pr_number`: the attribute name of a meta key. */\n+export function attributeName(key) {\n+  return `adl.${String(key).replace(/([a-z0-9])([A-Z])/g, '$1_$2').toLowerCase()}`;\n+}\n+\n+const isObj = (v) => v !== null && typeof v === 'object' && !Array.isArray(v);\n+const iso = (v) => (typeof v === 'string' && !Number.isNaN(Date.parse(v)) ? new Date(v).toISOString() : null);\n+const metaAttributes = (meta) => (isObj(meta) ? Object.fromEntries(Object.entries(meta).map(([k, v]) => [attributeName(k), v])) : {});\n+const outcomeStatus = (outcome) => (outcome === 'failed' ? 'error' : outcome == null ? 'unset' : 'ok');\n+const minIso = (a, b) => (!a ? b : !b ? a : a < b ? a : b);\n+const maxIso = (a, b) => (!a ? b : !b ? a : a > b ? a : b);\n+\n+/**\n+ * The span tree of a trace file (schema 1 or 2), parents before children, siblings by start time\n+ * (runners' clocks differ: only start order is meaningful across runs). Spans of a v1 trace, which\n+ * recorded no ids, get ids derived from the run id and stage. Unknown parent → the root.\n+ * Returns `{ rootSpanId, spans: [{ span_id, parent_span_id, name, kind, start, end, status, attributes, events }] }`.\n+ */\n+export function buildSpanTree(trace) {\n+  const t = isObj(trace) ? trace : {};\n+  const runKey = String(t.envelope?.run_id ?? t.run_id ?? 'unknown');\n+  const validId = (v) => (typeof v === 'string' && SPAN_ID_RE.test(v) ? v : null);\n+  const rootId = validId(t.root_span_id) ?? derivedSpanId(`${runKey}:root`);\n+  const events = (Array.isArray(t.events) ? t.events : []).filter(isObj);\n+\n+  const env = isObj(t.envelope) ? t.envelope : {};\n+  const item = isObj(t.item) ? t.item : {};\n+  const root = {\n+    span_id: rootId,\n+    parent_span_id: null,\n+    name: 'run',\n+    kind: 'internal',\n+    start: iso(t.started_at),\n+    end: iso(t.completed_at),\n+    status: outcomeStatus(t.outcome ?? null),\n+    attributes: {\n+      'adl.item.kind': item.kind ?? null,\n+      'adl.item.number': item.number ?? null,\n+      'adl.item.source': item.source ?? null,\n+      'cicd.pipeline.name': env.workflow ?? null,\n+      'cicd.pipeline.run.id': env.run_id ?? null,\n+      'adl.run.attempt': env.run_attempt ?? null,\n+      'adl.event_name': env.event_name ?? null,\n+      'adl.actor_type': env.actor_type ?? null,\n+      'adl.issue_number': env.issue_number ?? null,\n+      'vcs.change.id': env.pr_number ?? null,\n+      'vcs.ref.head.revision': env.head_sha ?? null,\n+      'adl.outcome': t.outcome ?? null,\n+    },\n+    events: [],\n+  };\n+  const spans = [root];\n+  const byId = new Map([[rootId, root]]);\n+  const add = (span) => {\n+    if (byId.has(span.span_id)) return;\n+    byId.set(span.span_id, span);\n+    spans.push(span);\n+  };\n+\n+  for (const s of (Array.isArray(t.spans) ? t.spans : []).filter(isObj)) {\n+    const start = iso(s.started_at);\n+    add({\ndiff --git a/scripts/tests/item_lineage.test.mjs b/scripts/tests/item_lineage.test.mjs\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000..1a2b3c4\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/scripts/tests/item_lineage.test.mjs\n@@ -0,0 +1,40 @@\n+// ADR-0063: trace identity — deterministic trace id per work item, resolution order, hostile PR text.\n+import { test } from 'node:test';\n+import assert from 'node:assert/strict';\n+import { createHash } from 'node:crypto';\n+\n+import {\n+  traceIdFor, derivedSpanId, newSpanId, branchIssue, closingIssues, payloadWorkItemHint, prWorkItemHint,\n+  resolveWorkItem, workItem, TRACE_ID_RE, SPAN_ID_RE, MAX_SCANNED_CHARS, MAX_CLOSING_REFS,\n+} from '../lib/item_lineage.mjs';\n+\n+const REPO = 'owner/repo';\n+\n+test('traceIdFor: 32 lowercase hex, the first 128 bits of SHA-256 of the key, stable across calls', () => {\n+  const id = traceIdFor(`${REPO}#issue-12`);\n+  assert.match(id, TRACE_ID_RE);\n+  assert.equal(id, createHash('sha256').update(`${REPO}#issue-12`).digest('hex').slice(0, 32));\n+  assert.equal(id, traceIdFor(`${REPO}#issue-12`));\n+  assert.notEqual(id, traceIdFor(`${REPO}#pr-12`));\n+  assert.notEqual(id, traceIdFor(`other/repo#issue-12`));\n+});\n+\n+test('span ids: 16 hex, random ones differ, derived ones are stable, an all-zero id is never produced', () => {\n+  assert.match(newSpanId(), SPAN_ID_RE);\n+  assert.notEqual(newSpanId(), newSpanId());\n+  assert.equal(newSpanId(() => Buffer.alloc(8)), '0000000000000001', 'W3C: all-zero is invalid');\n+  assert.equal(derivedSpanId('a'), derivedSpanId('a'));\n+  assert.match(derivedSpanId('a'), SPAN_ID_RE);\n+  assert.notEqual(derivedSpanId('a'), derivedSpanId('b'));\n+});\n+\n+test('branchIssue: only ai/issue-<n>, with or without refs/heads/', () => {\n+  assert.equal(branchIssue('ai/issue-42'), 42);\n+  assert.equal(branchIssue('refs/heads/ai/issue-7'), 7);\n+  for (const ref of ['ai/issue-', 'ai/issue-4x', 'feature/ai/issue-4', 'ai/issue-0', 'ai/issue-1234567890', null, 5, `ai/issue-1${'0'.repeat(300)}`]) {\n+    assert.equal(branchIssue(ref), null, String(ref));\n+  }\n+});\n+\n+test('closingIssues: GitHub closing keywords, body order, dedup, same-repository refs only', () => {\n+  assert.deepEqual(closingIssues('Closes #12'), [12]);\ndiff --git a/scripts/tests/lineage_spans.test.mjs b/scripts/tests/lineage_spans.test.mjs\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000..1a2b3c4\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/scripts/tests/lineage_spans.test.mjs\n@@ -0,0 +1,40 @@\n+// ADR-0063: span tree of a run (parents, ordering, retries, fallback, side effects) and its OTLP JSON\n+// encoding, validated against a minimal OTLP/JSON fixture so an export needs no remodeling.\n+import { test } from 'node:test';\n+import assert from 'node:assert/strict';\n+import fs from 'node:fs';\n+import path from 'node:path';\n+import { fileURLToPath } from 'node:url';\n+\n+import {\n+  buildSpanTree, toOtlpSpan, toOtlpDocument, toOtlpValue, toOtlpAttributes, unixNano, attributeName,\n+  SIDE_EFFECT_EVENTS, SPAN_KIND, STATUS_CODE,\n+} from '../lib/lineage_spans.mjs';\n+import { derivedSpanId, SPAN_ID_RE, TRACE_ID_RE } from '../lib/item_lineage.mjs';\n+\n+const FIXTURE = JSON.parse(fs.readFileSync(path.join(path.dirname(fileURLToPath(import.meta.url)), 'fixtures', 'otlp', 'minimal-trace.json'), 'utf8'));\n+const TRACE_ID = 'a'.repeat(32);\n+const ROOT = '1'.repeat(16);\n+const STAGE = '2'.repeat(16);\n+const LLM = '3'.repeat(16);\n+\n+// Structural check against the fixture: every key we emit exists at the same path in the fixture,\n+// with the same JSON type (arrays: the union of the fixture's elements).\n+const kind = (v) => (Array.isArray(v) ? 'array' : v === null ? 'null' : typeof v);\n+function merged(list) {\n+  const out = {};\n+  for (const el of list) for (const [k, v] of Object.entries(el)) out[k] = k in out && kind(out[k]) === 'array' ? [...out[k], ...v] : (k in out && kind(out[k]) === 'object' ? merged([out[k], v]) : v);\n+  return out;\n+}\n+function assertShape(value, ref, at = '$') {\n+  assert.equal(kind(value), kind(ref), `${at}: ${kind(value)} where the OTLP fixture has ${kind(ref)}`);\n+  if (Array.isArray(ref)) {\n+    const objects = ref.filter((r) => kind(r) === 'object');\n+    value.forEach((v, i) => assertShape(v, objects.length ? merged(objects) : ref[0], `${at}[${i}]`));\n+  } else if (kind(ref) === 'object') {\n+    for (const [k, v] of Object.entries(value)) {\n+      assert.ok(k in ref, `${at}.${k} is not an OTLP field`);\n+      // KeyValue lists share one shape (resource, span and event attributes): the fixture's union.\n+      assertShape(v, k === 'attributes' ? ATTRIBUTES_REF : ref[k], `${at}.${k}`);\n+    }\n+  }\ndiff --git a/scripts/reset_auto_fix.mjs b/scripts/reset_auto_fix.mjs\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000..1a2b3c4\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/scripts/reset_auto_fix.mjs\n@@ -0,0 +1,40 @@\n+#!/usr/bin/env node\n+/**\n+ * reset-auto-fix.yml (workflow_dispatch): removes the auto-fix-attempt-N labels of a PR and, with\n+ * RETRIGGER=true, removes then re-applies changes-requested so a fresh `labeled` event starts a new\n+ * auto-fix cycle. Instrumented like the other stages (ADR-0018, ADR-0062) so the run joins the trace\n+ * of the PR's work item (ADR-0063): the PR is read once for its head ref and closing references.\n+ * Env: GITHUB_TOKEN, GITHUB_REPOSITORY, PR_NUMBER, RETRIGGER, GITHUB_API_URL (optional), GITHUB_RUN_ID.\n+ */\n+import { readFileSync } from 'node:fs';\n+import path from 'node:path';\n+import { fileURLToPath } from 'node:url';\n+import { parseNestedYaml } from './lib/yaml.mjs';\n+import { log as obsLog, createTracer } from './lib/observability.mjs';\n+import { prWorkItemHint } from './lib/item_lineage.mjs';\n+\n+const STAGE = 'autofix_reset';\n+\n+/** Attempt labels and the changes-requested label from config/labels.yaml. */\n+export function resetLabels(labelsYaml) {\n+  const labels = parseNestedYaml(labelsYaml);\n+  return {\n+    attemptLabels: [labels.autofix.attempt1.name, labels.autofix.attempt2.name, labels.autofix.attempt3.name],\n+    changesLabel: labels.review.changes.name,\n+  };\n+}\n+\n+/**\n+ * The reset itself. `request(method, path, body?)` resolves `{ status, ok, json? }`; any non-404\n+ * failure throws. Returns `{ removed: [labels], retriggered: boolean }`.\n+ */\n+export async function resetAutoFix({ request, prNumber, retrigger, attemptLabels, changesLabel }) {\n+  const call = async (method, apiPath, body) => {\n+    const res = await request(method, apiPath, body);\n+    if (!res.ok && res.status !== 404) throw new Error(`GitHub API ${method} ${apiPath} → ${res.status}`);\n+    return res;\n+  };\n+  const pr = await call('GET', `/pulls/${prNumber}`);\n+  if (pr.ok) obsLog({ stage: STAGE, event: 'trace.work_item', level: 'info', meta: prWorkItemHint(pr.json) });\n+\n+  const removed = [];\ndiff --git a/.claude/skills/test-protocol/SKILL.md b/.claude/skills/test-protocol/SKILL.md\nindex 5d6e7f8..9a0b1c2 100644\n--- a/.claude/skills/test-protocol/SKILL.md\n+++ b/.claude/skills/test-protocol/SKILL.md\n@@ -62,6 +62,8 @@ Modules with CI-enforced ≥ 80% coverage (`c8 --check-coverage` in `test.yml`):\n - `scripts/lib/generation_stopped.mjs`\n - `scripts/lib/job_journal.mjs`\n - `scripts/lib/job_record.mjs`\n+- `scripts/lib/item_lineage.mjs`\n+- `scripts/lib/lineage_spans.mjs`\n - `scripts/build_eval_site.mjs` (entrypoint, measured with `build_eval_site.test.mjs`)\n \n Specific required paths for `scripts/lib/prompts.mjs`:\ndiff --git a/CHANGELOG.md b/CHANGELOG.md\nindex 5d6e7f8..9a0b1c2 100644\n--- a/CHANGELOG.md\n+++ b/CHANGELOG.md\n@@ -6,6 +6,7 @@ The format follows [Keep a Changelog](https://keepachangelog.com/en/1.0.0/).\n Entries are grouped by date. Add new entries under `[Unreleased]`.\n \n ## [Unreleased]\n+- End-to-end tracing per work item (ADR-0063). **Identity:** new pure `scripts/lib/item_lineage.mjs`: `trace_id` = 32-hex SHA-256 prefix of `<repo>#issue-<n>` (else `#pr-<n>`, else `#run-<run_id>`), resolved issue event → branch `ai/issue-<n>` → first closing reference of the PR body → PR → run; untrusted PR text parsed for same-repo `#<digits>` only (64 KiB, 20 refs), numbers kept, body never stored; `pr_review.mjs` and the new `scripts/reset_auto_fix.mjs` log `trace.work_item` from the PR they fetch. **Spans:** the trace file (`schema_version: 2`) gets `trace_id`, `item`, `root_span_id`, span ids on stage spans, `span_id` on every event, and `child_spans` (≤ 500, overflow counted); new `withSpan()` export of `observability.mjs` (AsyncLocalStorage); `callLLM()` wraps each call in an `llm_call` span with OpenTelemetry GenAI attributes (estimated tokens flagged `adl.usage.estimated`, fallback, per-provider outcome, input-budget skip, `error.type`), retries and fallback logged inside it; `runSuite()` adds an `eval.case` span per case × repeat. **Record:** `schema_version: 2` adds `trace_id`, `item`, span ids and `otlp` (OTLP/JSON `resourceSpans`, built by new `scripts/lib/lineage_spans.mjs`, validated against an OTLP fixture), span attributes through the per-span-name `SPAN_ATTRIBUTE_ALLOWLIST`, OTLP block ≤ 128 KiB (`spans_overflow`); `readRunRecord()` still reads v1. **Index:** `metrics/traces/<trace_id>.json` (runs, lead time) written by `commit_job_record.mjs` in the same commit as the record, same retry and dedup; an unreadable index is left untouched with a warning. **reset-auto-fix:** inline script moved to `scripts/reset_auto_fix.mjs` (`autofix_reset.*` events), trace artifact and \"Commit metrics\" (record only; `contents: write`). New modules under the c8 ≥ 80% gate (`test.yml`, `prompts/pr-review-system.md` gate (c) list, `eval-replay.yml` paths). Docs: `docs/observability.md` (trace model, attribute table, reading a trace), `docs/runbook.md` (find the trace of an issue).\n - Review eval dataset learns from production misjudgments. **Dataset** (`evals/datasets/review.jsonl`, sha changes): 5 incident cases, each with `source: \"PR #n\"` and the real diff reduced to its minimum — `incident-note-instead-of-fix` (#191/#196, `REQUEST_CHANGES`), `incident-stale-refs-shared-phrasing` (#207, `APPROVE`, regression case for #212), `incident-toctou-untested-claim` (#194, `REQUEST_CHANGES`, `known-gap`), `incident-finding-on-cut-hunks` (#187, `APPROVE`, ADR-0034), `incident-clean-code-cut` (#206, `WITHHELD`, ADR-0038); floor 23 → 27 gated cases, 4 new pins. **Context parity:** review cases take optional precomputed `stale_refs` / `related_adrs` / `prompt_budget` (ADR-0035/0036/0037), passed to `buildReviewPrompt` through the formatters `pr_review.mjs` uses; `eval_suites.test.mjs` fails when `pr_review.mjs` passes a `buildReviewPrompt` field the suite does not, or formats it differently. **`known-gap` tag** (ADR-0031 amendment §7): run, scored and published (`summary.known_gap`, run page), excluded from the gated metrics and the floor count, shown in the report (`formatReport`), the run page and the scorecard entry (`known_gap`); `eval_threshold_floor.test.mjs` pins every other case, so removing the tag is the only way in and a gated case can never be tagged. **Prompt:** `pr-review-system.md` reports a PR that touches no code for a code issue as a HIGH \"not implemented\" (+110 tokens, headroom 55%). **Process:** AGENTS.md → Eval Gates: a production misjudgment gets a case in its fix PR or an `eval-case` issue; `docs/evals.md` gets an incident backlog for generation / autofix. Review `tokensPerRunEst` 4200 → 5300; replay fixture extended with the 5 cases; `eval-replay.yml` paths add `prompt_budget.mjs`.\n - Live `review` evals on Groq produce a result again. `run_evals.mjs` called `callLLM` without `responseFormat`, so `groq_client.mjs` sent its `json_object` default and Groq rejected the Markdown review with `400 Failed to generate JSON`: on run 38561304861, 4 of 40 calls answered before the TPD circuit breaker tripped, and the failed calls spent the daily quota. Every suite in `scripts/lib/eval_suites.mjs` now declares `llmCall` — the `loadLLMConfig` fields and literal `callLLM` options of its production stage (`review`: `responseFormat: null`, no `maxInputTokens`, as `pr_review.mjs`; `validation`: the `validate_issue.mjs` call, `json_object` default kept) — and the live eval LLM forwards only those (`liveCallArgs` / `createLiveLLM`, exported from `run_evals.mjs`; `buildLLM` exported). Before, the review eval also passed `maxInputTokens`, which production does not. New parity test in `eval_suites.test.mjs` parses the `callLLM({ … })` call sites of `pr_review.mjs` and `validate_issue.mjs` and fails when a suite disagrees; mocked-fetch tests assert the review payload has no `response_format` and the validation payload `json_object`; replay unchanged. Production stages unchanged. `docs/evals.md`: Groq `review` results up to and including 38561304861 are not a model measurement.\n - Every action of the pipeline agent is recorded durably for a dashboard (ADR-0062, capture + storage only). **Events:** missing side effects now emit events through `observability.mjs` — `issue_validation.comment_posted` / `labels_applied`, `code_gen.context_built` / `escalated`, `review.evidence_assessed` / `prompt_truncated` / `comment_posted` / `review_submitted` / `labels_applied`, `autofix.reset` / `prompt_budget` / `attempt_labeled` / `escalated`, `autofix.skipped` reasons `untrusted_comment` and `self_modification`, `retry.wait` (`retry.mjs`), `llm_call` / `llm_call_failed` (`callLLM()`: provider and model that answered, fallback flag), `workflow.pr_operation` / `workflow.push`. **Run journal:** new `scripts/lib/job_journal.mjs`: the trace file keeps every `log()` event (`events[]`, ≤ 500 events / 256 KiB, overflow counted in `events_overflow`), `schema_version: 1` and a run `envelope` (workflow, run id/attempt, trigger, actor type, issue/PR, head SHA, provider/model per LLM call, run/PR/issue/comment URLs); event and span meta strings are scrubbed in the process that writes the trace (its env holds the LLM keys, the committing step's does not); a trace already at the path is adopted only when its envelope names this run and attempt (a file committed in the PR head is replaced); `finalize()` writes synchronously; `log()` and `createTracer()` signatures unchanged, stdout and the stderr line untouched. **Public record:** new `scripts/lib/job_record.mjs`: `redactTrace()` — per-event meta allowlist, env values and credential shapes scrubbed, strings ≤ 200 chars, nested objects dropped. **Persistence:** new entrypoint `scripts/commit_job_record.mjs` replaces the shell of the four \"Commit metrics\" steps: `runs.jsonl` lines + `metrics/runs/<YYYY-MM>/<run_id>-<attempt>.json` in one commit on `metrics` (Git Data API, fast-forward only, 3 attempts), first record per run attempt wins; `code-generation.yml` passes the `create-pull-request` outputs, `auto-fix-pr.yml` the push outcome. Retention ≈ 2–6 MB/month, 12 months (runbook). ADR-0013 amended. Both new modules are under the `test.yml` c8 ≥ 80% gate (listed in `prompts/pr-review-system.md` gate (c)). Renumbered from ADR-0039, taken on `main` by the LangGraph prototype (#214); `related_adrs.test.mjs` now fails on two `docs/adr/` files sharing a number (`findRelatedAdrs()` keys ADRs by number). `GITHUB_WORKFLOW_SHA` is public run metadata (a push-triggered head SHA was redacted). In `pr-review.yml` / `auto-fix-pr.yml`, \"Commit metrics\" warns and exits 0 when the trusted default-branch copy has no `commit_job_record.mjs` yet (this PR's own runs), instead of failing the job.\ndiff --git a/docs/testing.md b/docs/testing.md\nindex 5d6e7f8..9a0b1c2 100644\n--- a/docs/testing.md\n+++ b/docs/testing.md\n@@ -49,8 +49,10 @@ Requires Node.js 20+. All tests should pass in under a few seconds.\n | `scripts/lib/prompt_budget.mjs` | 20 | Prompt → stage mapping (checked against `config/models.yaml`), placeholder-free token count, input vs TPM budget (unset or invalid → null), changed-prompt detection (new, deleted, nested and non-prompt paths ignored), prompt grows, shrinks, new (no base read), deleted (no head read), no budget configured, unmapped prompt, prompt shared by several stages, `auto-fix-system.md` on the TPM window, 10% threshold crossed or not and configurable, read error (warn event, empty result), prompt block and comment table. CI-enforced ≥ 80% via c8 |\n | `scripts/lib/event_docs.mjs` | 10 | Event-docs check (#198): literal event names in single/double/backtick quotes, dynamic `${…}` names and non-event keys ignored, table-row first cell only (prose, lists and other cells ignored), missing events sorted with every emitting file, nothing missing / nothing emitted; entrypoint `check_event_docs.mjs`: pass (tests and non-`.mjs` files skipped), fail listing events and files, missing doc → exit 1. CI-enforced ≥ 80% via c8 |\n | `scripts/lib/generation_stopped.mjs` | 34 | Generation \"blocked\" outcome (ADR-0029 amendment): needed paths (URLs, root `CHANGELOG.md` and bare names of named paths dropped; bare names only when at the root), deterministic block on the abridged #190 / #195 bodies, withheld path, one writable path or no path → not blocked; `blocked` must be the boolean `true` (summary text, `null`, `false` ignored; `\"true\"`, `1` throw); labels as JSON or comma list; notes-only refusal (bug/feature only, any non-Markdown file, existing file or `docs/` → allowed); precedence deterministic > model > notes-only, planned fix from `planned_fix` / note content / summary, capped; comment format; `escalateBlocked` call order, 422 / 404 tolerated, each failed call throws. Entrypoint branches in `smoke.test.mjs`. CI-enforced ≥ 80% via c8 |\n-| `scripts/lib/job_journal.mjs` | 27 | Run journal (ADR-0062): event order next to spans, adoption of pre-tracer events, cross-process append of the same run, a trace from another run / attempt / without envelope replaced (no forged events, spans, links), count and byte caps with `events_overflow`, oversized event, circular meta, event and span meta scrubbed of the producing process's env (secret absent from the committer env never reaches the record), event logged during `finalize()` kept, stdout untouched, one `trace_write_failed`, missing directory / half-written trace, envelope (env, payload, bot actor, meta fallback, links, `llm_calls`). CI-enforced ≥ 80% via c8 |\n-| `scripts/lib/job_record.mjs` | 21 | Public-safety contract: planted env secret and prompt body never survive, credential shapes, `scrubString` (no cut) vs `redactString` (scrub then cut), allowlist free of prompt/body/env keys, unlisted event → `meta {}`, nested objects dropped, URLs pinned to `GITHUB_SERVER_URL`, `GITHUB_WORKFLOW_SHA` public, 256 KiB cap, Git Data API commit (single commit, dedup per run attempt, ref race retry, give-up, every failure branch). CI-enforced ≥ 80% via c8 |\n+| `scripts/lib/job_journal.mjs` | 33 | Run journal (ADR-0062): event order next to spans, adoption of pre-tracer events, cross-process append of the same run, a trace from another run / attempt / without envelope replaced (no forged events, spans, links), count and byte caps with `events_overflow`, oversized event, circular meta, event and span meta scrubbed of the producing process's env (secret absent from the committer env never reaches the record), event logged during `finalize()` kept, stdout untouched, one `trace_write_failed`, missing directory / half-written trace, envelope (env, payload, bot actor, meta fallback, links, `llm_calls`); span context (ADR-0063): stage span ids under the root, `span_id` on every event, nested / failing / concurrent `withSpan()`, 500-span cap counted, root and child spans adopted from an earlier step only, work item from the payload (body never kept) and `trace.work_item`. CI-enforced ≥ 80% via c8 |\n+| `scripts/lib/job_record.mjs` | 31 | Public-safety contract: planted env secret and prompt body never survive, credential shapes, `scrubString` (no cut) vs `redactString` (scrub then cut), allowlist free of prompt/body/env keys, unlisted event → `meta {}`, nested objects dropped, URLs pinned to `GITHUB_SERVER_URL`, `GITHUB_WORKFLOW_SHA` public, 256 KiB cap, Git Data API commit (single commit, dedup per run attempt, ref race retry, give-up, every failure branch); schema 2 (ADR-0063): trace id / item recomputed (never copied), OTLP block with parents and GenAI attributes, planted secret / env value / prompt body in span attributes dropped or scrubbed, per-span-name allowlist, 128 KiB OTLP cap counted without orphans, v1 trace and record read, trace index (dedup, order, lead time, overflow, foreign index refused) committed with the record (same commit, read error retried, unreadable index left as is). CI-enforced ≥ 80% via c8 |\n+| `scripts/lib/item_lineage.mjs` | 11 | Trace identity (ADR-0063): trace id = SHA-256 prefix of the item key (W3C, never all-zero), random and derived span ids, `ai/issue-<n>` branch parsing, closing keywords in body order / dedup / same-repo only, hostile body bounded (64 KiB scanned, 20 refs, linear time), payload hints for every trigger (issue, dispatch, PR, PR comment, push), resolution order and conflicts (branch beats body, first of several issues), one trace per item across all workflows. CI-enforced ≥ 80% via c8 |\n+| `scripts/lib/lineage_spans.mjs` | 9 | Span tree (ADR-0063): root → stage → `llm_call`, side effects as child spans, retries / fallback as span events of the LLM span, start-time ordering, v1 trace ids derived, forged cycles and unknown parents re-attached to the root; OTLP JSON encoding validated against `fixtures/otlp/minimal-trace.json`, every AnyValue form. CI-enforced ≥ 80% via c8 |\n | `scripts/lib/eval_harness.mjs` | 25 | Dataset parsing (invalid JSON, missing fields, duplicate ids, empty), tag/limit filtering, call recording, replay (ordering, exhausted queue, recorded-error rethrow), runner (scores, errored runs, repeats, concurrency order), percentile, confusion matrix, per-class P/R/F1, consistency, summary, thresholds, report. CI-enforced ≥ 80% via c8 |\n | `scripts/lib/eval_scorecard.mjs` | 23 | Scorecard read (missing file, unsupported format, invalid JSON), run conversion (defaults, replay rejection), history ordering/dedup/cap, deltas, dataset-hash Δ suppression, error_rate publish filter, Markdown rendering, README marker helpers, and that the README links the Pages dashboard with no committed scorecard view left. CI-enforced ≥ 80% via c8 |\n | `scripts/lib/eval_site.mjs` | 21 | HTML/script escaping, shields endpoint badge (incl. a registered suite with no published run → grey `no run yet`), threshold rendering, trend chart (≥ 2 runs, missing values, zoomed y domain, textContent-only tooltip), index (empty state, Δ, dataset change, failed gate, several suites with their own gate, trend and badge), run page (confusion matrix, escaped model output), site file map. CI-enforced ≥ 80% via c8 |\ndiff --git a/scripts/tests/workflow_gates.test.mjs b/scripts/tests/workflow_gates.test.mjs\nindex 5d6e7f8..9a0b1c2 100644\n--- a/scripts/tests/workflow_gates.test.mjs\n+++ b/scripts/tests/workflow_gates.test.mjs\n@@ -7,7 +7,7 @@ import { fileURLToPath } from 'node:url';\n const ROOT = resolve(dirname(fileURLToPath(import.meta.url)), '../..');\n const workflow = readFileSync(resolve(ROOT, '.github/workflows/test.yml'), 'utf8');\n \n-const GATED_MODULES = ['checkpoint.mjs', 'config.mjs', 'llm_client.mjs', 'anthropic_client.mjs', 'groq_client.mjs', 'output_writer.mjs', 'review_evidence.mjs', 'eval_harness.mjs', 'eval_scorecard.mjs', 'eval_site.mjs', 'eval_suites.mjs', 'review_prompt.mjs', 'eval_replay_ci.mjs', 'pr_evals.mjs', 'static_verifier.mjs', 'issue_validator.mjs', 'stale_refs.mjs', 'related_adrs.mjs', 'prompt_budget.mjs', 'event_docs.mjs', 'generation_stopped.mjs', 'job_journal.mjs', 'job_record.mjs'];\n+const GATED_MODULES = ['checkpoint.mjs', 'config.mjs', 'llm_client.mjs', 'anthropic_client.mjs', 'groq_client.mjs', 'output_writer.mjs', 'review_evidence.mjs', 'eval_harness.mjs', 'eval_scorecard.mjs', 'eval_site.mjs', 'eval_suites.mjs', 'review_prompt.mjs', 'eval_replay_ci.mjs', 'pr_evals.mjs', 'static_verifier.mjs', 'issue_validator.mjs', 'stale_refs.mjs', 'related_adrs.mjs', 'prompt_budget.mjs', 'event_docs.mjs', 'generation_stopped.mjs', 'job_journal.mjs', 'job_record.mjs', 'item_lineage.mjs', 'lineage_spans.mjs'];\n \n // Entrypoints (scripts/*.mjs) under the same gate, measured through their own test file.\n const GATED_ENTRYPOINTS = [['build_eval_site.mjs', 'build_eval_site.test.mjs']];\n@@ -71,6 +71,8 @@ test('test.yml pairs each coverage gate with its dedicated test file', () => {\n     ['prompt_budget.mjs', 'prompt_budget.test.mjs'],\n     ['job_journal.mjs', 'job_journal.test.mjs'],\n     ['job_record.mjs', 'job_record.test.mjs'],\n+    ['item_lineage.mjs', 'item_lineage.test.mjs'],\n+    ['lineage_spans.mjs', 'lineage_spans.test.mjs'],\n   ];\n   for (const [lib, testFile] of pairs) {\n     assert.ok(workflow.includes(`scripts/lib/${lib}`), `Missing lib reference: ${lib}`);\n@@ -175,9 +177,11 @@ test('auto-fix-pr.yml does not write the raw multi-line PR payload to GITHUB_OUT\n // branch must come from a file outside it, never from the working-tree metrics/runs.jsonl.\n test('workflows that commit metrics read them from $RUNNER_TEMP, not the checkout', () => {\n   const committing = readWorkflows().filter(({ text }) => text.includes('name: Commit metrics'));\n-  assert.deepEqual(committing.map((w) => w.name).sort(), ['auto-fix-pr.yml', 'code-generation.yml', 'pr-review.yml', 'validate-issue.yml']);\n+  assert.deepEqual(committing.map((w) => w.name).sort(), ['auto-fix-pr.yml', 'code-generation.yml', 'pr-review.yml', 'reset-auto-fix.yml', 'validate-issue.yml']);\n   for (const { name, text } of committing) {\n     assert.ok(!/(wc -l|tail|cat)[^\\n]*metrics\\/runs\\.jsonl/.test(text), `${name} must not read the working-tree metrics file`);\n+    // ADR-0063: reset-auto-fix writes no runs.jsonl line, only its run record and the trace index.\n+    if (name === 'reset-auto-fix.yml') { assert.ok(!text.includes('METRICS_FILE'), `${name}: record only`); continue; }\n     const envLines = text.match(/METRICS_FILE: \\$\\{\\{ runner\\.temp \\}\\}\\/pipeline-metrics\\.jsonl/g) ?? [];\n     assert.ok(envLines.length >= 2, `${name} must pass METRICS_FILE under runner.temp to the script and to \"Commit metrics\"`);\n   }\n@@ -192,7 +196,7 @@ test('workflows that commit metrics read and write the metrics branch, never the\n   assert.equal(METRICS_BRANCH, 'metrics');\n   assert.equal(RUNS_JSONL_PATH, 'metrics/runs.jsonl');\n   const committing = readWorkflows().filter(({ text }) => text.includes('name: Commit metrics'));\n-  assert.equal(committing.length, 4);\n+  assert.equal(committing.length, 5);\n   for (const { name, text } of committing) {\n     const step = text.slice(text.indexOf('- name: Commit metrics')).split(/\\n      - name: /)[0];\n     const trusted = BRANCH_TRIGGERED_SECRET_WORKFLOWS.includes(name);\ndiff --git a/docs/observability.md b/docs/observability.md\nindex 5d6e7f8..9a0b1c2 100644\n--- a/docs/observability.md\n+++ b/docs/observability.md\n@@ -136,6 +136,18 @@ The `evidence` and `review` jobs share one `GITHUB_RUN_ID`, so the evidence trac\n | `autofix.skipped`              | info / warn | ✓        | `reason` (`untrusted_comment`, info: before the tracer, stderr only \\| `self_modification`, warn: the PR changes `auto_fix_pr.mjs`, comment posted (`url`) \\| `approved`, info: no LLM call \\| `no_changes`, warn: attempt consumed, `needs-human` applied, summary commented, `autofix_skip` metric \\| `guardrail_rejected`, warn: same, with the rejection reason commented — write denylist, shrink guard, ADR-0029 write guard or ADR-0019 static rules; `rules` lists them), `attempt`, `prNumber`, `headSha` (approved only) — exit 0, nothing pushed (ADR-0028) |\n | `autofix.error`                | error  | ✓             | `error`, `attempt`, `prNumber`            |\n \n+### `autofix_reset`\n+\n+Emitted by `scripts/reset_auto_fix.mjs` (`reset-auto-fix.yml`, ADR-0063): the reset joins the trace of the PR's work item.\n+\n+| Event                          | Level | `duration_ms` | Key `meta` fields |\n+|--------------------------------|-------|---------------|-------------------|\n+| `autofix_reset.start`          | info  | —             | `prNumber` |\n+| `autofix_reset.labels_removed` | info  | —             | `prNumber`, `removed_labels` |\n+| `autofix_reset.retriggered`    | info  | —             | `prNumber`, `label` — changes-requested removed and re-applied (new `labeled` event) |\n+| `autofix_reset.complete`       | info  | ✓             | `prNumber`, `retrigger` |\n+| `autofix_reset.error`          | error | ✓             | `prNumber`, `error` |\n+\n ### `eval`\n \n Emitted by `run_evals.mjs` (ADR-0027).\n@@ -205,6 +217,14 @@ Emitted by `commit_job_record.mjs` (\"Commit metrics\") for what a workflow step d\n | `workflow.pr_operation` | info        | —             | `prNumber`, `operation` (`created` \\| `updated` \\| `closed` \\| `none`), `url` — `peter-evans/create-pull-request` outputs (code-generation) |\n | `workflow.push`         | info / warn | —             | `prNumber`, `outcome` (`success` \\| `failure` \\| `skipped`) — the auto-fix \"Commit and push fixes\" step; warn on failure |\n \n+### `trace`\n+\n+Emitted by scripts that read a PR whose payload lacks its body or head ref (push-triggered `pr_review.mjs`, `reset_auto_fix.mjs`), so the run resolves the same work item as the others (ADR-0063).\n+\n+| Event              | Level | `duration_ms` | Key `meta` fields |\n+|--------------------|-------|---------------|-------------------|\n+| `trace.work_item`  | info  | —             | `prNumber`, `branchIssue` (`ai/issue-<n>` head ref, else null), `closingIssues` (issues the body closes, body order, ≤ 20) — numbers only, the body is never logged |\n+\n ### `dependency_manifest`\n \n Emitted by `dependency_manifest.mjs` (#195, ADR-0023) in the review, code generation and auto-fix stages. The stage continues with no manifest.\n","evidence":{"version":1,"head_sha":"d8b1f3a5c7e9d0b2a4c6e8f0a1b3c5d7e9f1a3b5","generated_at":"2026-10-17T00:15:00Z","checks":[{"name":"tests","command":"npm test","status":"pass","exit_code":0,"duration_ms":31877,"output_tail":"# pass 1729\n# fail 0"},{"name":"lint","command":"npm run lint","status":"pass","exit_code":0,"duration_ms":1912,"output_tail":""}]},"head_sha":"d8b1f3a5c7e9d0b2a4c6e8f0a1b3c5d7e9f1a3b5","prompt_budget":[{"prompt":"prompts/pr-review-system.md","stage":"review","budget":"input","deltaTokens":16,"headTokens":2607,"maxInputTokens":6300,"headroomTokens":3455,"lowHeadroom":false}]},"expected":{"verdict":"WITHHELD"}}
{"id":"incident-untested-claim-symlink-dir","source":"PR #221","tags":["approve","clean","incident","untested-claim","pair"],"input":{"title":"feat(archive): list the monthly export files without following symlinks","body":"The nightly archiver uploads every `.csv` under `exports/<month>/`. `listExports(root)` returns those paths, sorted, and never follows a symlink: a symlinked `.csv` file and a symlinked month directory are both skipped, so the archiver cannot be pointed at files outside `exports/`. Unit tests added.\n\nCloses #44","diff":"diff --git a/src/export/list_exports.mjs b/src/export/list_exports.mjs\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000..7253823\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/src/export/list_exports.mjs\n@@ -0,0 +1,15 @@\n+import fs from 'node:fs';\n+import path from 'node:path';\n+\n+// Paths of the .csv files under <root>/<month>/, sorted. A symlink, file or month directory, is never followed.\n+export function listExports(root) {\n+  const out = [];\n+  for (const month of fs.readdirSync(root, { withFileTypes: true })) {\n+    if (!month.isDirectory()) continue;\n+    const dir = path.join(root, month.name);\n+    for (const file of fs.readdirSync(dir, { withFileTypes: true })) {\n+      if (file.isFile() && file.name.endsWith('.csv')) out.push(path.join(dir, file.name));\n+    }\n+  }\n+  return out.sort();\n+}\ndiff --git a/test/list_exports.test.mjs b/test/list_exports.test.mjs\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000..a253f18\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/test/list_exports.test.mjs\n@@ -0,0 +1,26 @@\n+import { test } from 'node:test';\n+import assert from 'node:assert/strict';\n+import fs from 'node:fs';\n+import os from 'node:os';\n+import path from 'node:path';\n+import { listExports } from '../src/export/list_exports.mjs';\n+\n+const tmpRoot = () => fs.mkdtempSync(path.join(os.tmpdir(), 'exports-'));\n+\n+test('listExports returns the .csv files of every month, sorted', () => {\n+  const root = tmpRoot();\n+  fs.mkdirSync(path.join(root, '2026-09'));\n+  fs.writeFileSync(path.join(root, '2026-09', 'b.csv'), 'id\\n');\n+  fs.writeFileSync(path.join(root, '2026-09', 'a.csv'), 'id\\n');\n+  fs.writeFileSync(path.join(root, '2026-09', 'notes.txt'), '');\n+  assert.deepEqual(listExports(root), [path.join(root, '2026-09', 'a.csv'), path.join(root, '2026-09', 'b.csv')]);\n+});\n+\n+test('listExports skips a symlinked .csv file', () => {\n+  const root = tmpRoot();\n+  fs.mkdirSync(path.join(root, '2026-09'));\n+  const outside = path.join(tmpRoot(), 'outside.csv');\n+  fs.writeFileSync(outside, 'id\\n');\n+  fs.symlinkSync(outside, path.join(root, '2026-09', 'link.csv'));\n+  assert.deepEqual(listExports(root), []);\n+});\n"},"expected":{"verdict":"APPROVE","must_advise":["untested claim|not exercised|no test covers","month director|symlinked director"]}}
{"id":"incident-tested-claim-symlink-dir","source":"PR #221","tags":["approve","clean","incident","untested-claim","pair"],"input":{"title":"feat(archive): list the monthly export files without following symlinks","body":"The nightly archiver uploads every `.csv` under `exports/<month>/`. `listExports(root)` returns those paths, sorted, and never follows a symlink: a symlinked `.csv` file and a symlinked month directory are both skipped, so the archiver cannot be pointed at files outside `exports/`. Unit tests added.\n\nCloses #44","diff":"diff --git a/src/export/list_exports.mjs b/src/export/list_exports.mjs\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000..7253823\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/src/export/list_exports.mjs\n@@ -0,0 +1,15 @@\n+import fs from 'node:fs';\n+import path from 'node:path';\n+\n+// Paths of the .csv files under <root>/<month>/, sorted. A symlink, file or month directory, is never followed.\n+export function listExports(root) {\n+  const out = [];\n+  for (const month of fs.readdirSync(root, { withFileTypes: true })) {\n+    if (!month.isDirectory()) continue;\n+    const dir = path.join(root, month.name);\n+    for (const file of fs.readdirSync(dir, { withFileTypes: true })) {\n+      if (file.isFile() && file.name.endsWith('.csv')) out.push(path.join(dir, file.name));\n+    }\n+  }\n+  return out.sort();\n+}\ndiff --git a/test/list_exports.test.mjs b/test/list_exports.test.mjs\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000..a253f18\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/test/list_exports.test.mjs\n@@ -0,0 +1,34 @@\n+import { test } from 'node:test';\n+import assert from 'node:assert/strict';\n+import fs from 'node:fs';\n+import os from 'node:os';\n+import path from 'node:path';\n+import { listExports } from '../src/export/list_exports.mjs';\n+\n+const tmpRoot = () => fs.mkdtempSync(path.join(os.tmpdir(), 'exports-'));\n+\n+test('listExports returns the .csv files of every month, sorted', () => {\n+  const root = tmpRoot();\n+  fs.mkdirSync(path.join(root, '2026-09'));\n+  fs.writeFileSync(path.join(root, '2026-09', 'b.csv'), 'id\\n');\n+  fs.writeFileSync(path.join(root, '2026-09', 'a.csv'), 'id\\n');\n+  fs.writeFileSync(path.join(root, '2026-09', 'notes.txt'), '');\n+  assert.deepEqual(listExports(root), [path.join(root, '2026-09', 'a.csv'), path.join(root, '2026-09', 'b.csv')]);\n+});\n+\n+test('listExports skips a symlinked .csv file', () => {\n+  const root = tmpRoot();\n+  fs.mkdirSync(path.join(root, '2026-09'));\n+  const outside = path.join(tmpRoot(), 'outside.csv');\n+  fs.writeFileSync(outside, 'id\\n');\n+  fs.symlinkSync(outside, path.join(root, '2026-09', 'link.csv'));\n+  assert.deepEqual(listExports(root), []);\n+});\n+\n+test('listExports skips a symlinked month directory', () => {\n+  const root = tmpRoot();\n+  const outside = tmpRoot();\n+  fs.writeFileSync(path.join(outside, 'secret.csv'), 'id\\n');\n+  fs.symlinkSync(outside, path.join(root, '2026-10'));\n+  assert.deepEqual(listExports(root), []);\n+});\n"},"expected":{"verdict":"APPROVE","must_not_flag":["untested claim|not exercised|no test covers"]}}
{"id":"clean-empty-body-no-claim","tags":["approve","clean","untested-claim"],"input":{"title":"feat(avatar): initials fallback when a user has no picture","body":"","diff":"diff --git a/src/avatar/initials.mjs b/src/avatar/initials.mjs\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000..69231da\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/src/avatar/initials.mjs\n@@ -0,0 +1,4 @@\n+// Upper-case initials of a display name: 'ada lovelace' -> 'AL'. Extra whitespace is ignored.\n+export function initials(displayName) {\n+  return displayName.trim().split(/\\s+/).filter(Boolean).map((part) => part[0].toUpperCase()).join('');\n+}\ndiff --git a/test/initials.test.mjs b/test/initials.test.mjs\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000..0a6b1f2\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/test/initials.test.mjs\n@@ -0,0 +1,13 @@\n+import { test } from 'node:test';\n+import assert from 'node:assert/strict';\n+import { initials } from '../src/avatar/initials.mjs';\n+\n+test('initials takes the first letter of each word, upper-cased', () => {\n+  assert.equal(initials('ada lovelace'), 'AL');\n+  assert.equal(initials('  grace   brewster hopper '), 'GBH');\n+});\n+\n+test('initials of an empty or blank name is empty', () => {\n+  assert.equal(initials(''), '');\n+  assert.equal(initials('   '), '');\n+});\n"},"expected":{"verdict":"APPROVE","must_not_flag":["untested claim|not exercised|no test covers"]}}
{"id":"docs-only-behavior-sentence","tags":["approve","clean","docs","untested-claim"],"input":{"title":"docs(uploader): explain UploadUnavailableError and the 503 retries","body":"Users keep asking why an upload fails after about 14 seconds. The uploader already retries a 503 three times (2 s, 4 s, 8 s) before it throws `UploadUnavailableError`, and no other 5xx is retried; this was never written down. The troubleshooting section now says so. No code change.\n\nCloses #91","diff":"diff --git a/docs/uploader.md b/docs/uploader.md\nindex 3c4d5e6..7f8a9b0 100644\n--- a/docs/uploader.md\n+++ b/docs/uploader.md\n@@ -31,4 +31,11 @@ ## Troubleshooting\n ### The upload stops with `UploadUnavailableError`\n \n-The storage service was unavailable.\n+The storage service answered 503 four times in a row. The uploader retries a 503 three times,\n+after 2 s, 4 s and 8 s, and gives up on the fourth answer; other 5xx responses are not retried.\n+\n+What to do:\n+\n+1. Check the storage status page.\n+2. Run the upload again once the service is back: files already stored are skipped.\n \n ### The upload is slow\n"},"expected":{"verdict":"APPROVE","must_not_flag":["untested claim|not exercised|no test covers"]}}
{"id":"truncated-claim-tests-past-cut","requires_cut":true,"tags":["approve","clean","budget-cut","untested-claim"],"input":{"title":"feat(retry): capped exponential backoff for the sync client","body":"`backoffMs(attempt, baseMs)` doubles the delay on each attempt from a 500 ms default and is capped at 30 s; an attempt that is not a positive integer throws `RangeError`. Table-driven tests over the 20 attempts and every base delay in use, plus the default and the `RangeError`.\n\nCloses #57","diff":"diff --git a/src/retry/backoff.mjs b/src/retry/backoff.mjs\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000..ac5f551\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/src/retry/backoff.mjs\n@@ -0,0 +1,7 @@\n+// Delay before retry `attempt` (1-based): baseMs doubled per attempt, capped at MAX_BACKOFF_MS.\n+export const MAX_BACKOFF_MS = 30000;\n+\n+export function backoffMs(attempt, baseMs = 500) {\n+  if (!Number.isInteger(attempt) || attempt < 1) throw new RangeError('attempt must be a positive integer');\n+  return Math.min(baseMs * 2 ** (attempt - 1), MAX_BACKOFF_MS);\n+}\ndiff --git a/test/backoff.test.mjs b/test/backoff.test.mjs\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000..b1a4f4f\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/test/backoff.test.mjs\n@@ -0,0 +1,283 @@\n+import { test } from 'node:test';\n+import assert from 'node:assert/strict';\n+import { backoffMs, MAX_BACKOFF_MS } from '../src/retry/backoff.mjs';\n+\n+// Every attempt of the 20 the client may make, for each base delay configured in a deployment.\n+const TABLE = [\n+  { attempt: 1, baseMs: 100, expectedMs: 100 }, // doubling: 100 x 2^0\n+  { attempt: 2, baseMs: 100, expectedMs: 200 }, // doubling: 100 x 2^1\n+  { attempt: 3, baseMs: 100, expectedMs: 400 }, // doubling: 100 x 2^2\n+  { attempt: 4, baseMs: 100, expectedMs: 800 }, // doubling: 100 x 2^3\n+  { attempt: 5, baseMs: 100, expectedMs: 1600 }, // doubling: 100 x 2^4\n+  { attempt: 6, baseMs: 100, expectedMs: 3200 }, // doubling: 100 x 2^5\n+  { attempt: 7, baseMs: 100, expectedMs: 6400 }, // doubling: 100 x 2^6\n